From 9f59ff3a80f726615947b91b6b797e86f0f47e81 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: joethedev5 <deepsbx1@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 05:41:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 45/45] Recover the ARM feature detection and Apple AIDR keys

xnu-13432 moved the EL0-visible ARM feature detection out of the
commpage and into osfmk/arm/arm_features.inc, where each feature is
enabled as a static_if key.  Reconstruct the whole file from the KDK
27.0.1 DWARF and both reference kernel images:

 - osfmk/arm64/cpu_features.c defines the Apple_* jump keys and pulls
   in the shared detection code.
 - osfmk/arm/arm_features.inc holds the per-register init routines
   (zfr0, isar0-3, mmfr0-2, pfr0-2, smfr0, fpcr, misc), the two
   static_if initializers, and the ARM_FEAT_* key definitions.
 - The ID-register tests mirror the public commpage code, extended with
   the new 13432 fields (ISAR1 PAuth_LR, ISAR2 LUT, ISAR3, MMFR0
   ASIDBits, MMFR2 VARANGE_EN, PFR1 CSV2_1p2, PFR2 FPMR, SMFR0
   LUTv2/F8F16/F8F32) and the Apple AIDR bits.
 - The old ARM_FEATURE_FLAG list moves to osfmk/arm/arm_features.h so
   commpage and kern_mib keep building.

Verified against the reference disassembly: the recovered code enables
the same 82 ARM feature keys and the same Apple keys, with matching
masks, thresholds and control flow.

Authored-By: joethedev5 <joeshmo@nunya.com>
---
 bsd/kern/kern_mib.c           |   4 +-
 osfmk/arm/Makefile            |   1 +
 osfmk/arm/arm_features.h      | 131 +++++
 osfmk/arm/arm_features.inc    | 865 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 osfmk/arm/commpage/commpage.c |   2 +-
